From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] rs6000: sign-extend the MI thunk vcall offset in the hybrid ABI

The Cell ELF64/ILP32 ABI has TARGET_64BIT with Pmode == SImode.
rs6000_output_mi_thunk loads the vtable pointer and then the vcall offset
in Pmode, which is lwz (zero-extending), and adds the offset to `this'
with a full-width add.  A virtual-base thunk's vcall offset is a signed
displacement and normally negative, so `this' reaches the target function
as this + 2^32 - k.  Seen at -O0 and at -O2 -fno-inline, where thunks take
this assembly path; -O2 and -Os otherwise expand the thunk through the
generic path, which already sign-extends (lwa) and canonicalizes.

Sign-extend the loaded offset (extsw) before the add.  The vtable pointer
stays zero-extended: it is an address.  extsw rather than lwa because the
rs6000 cell_micro attribute marks sign-extending loads as always
microcoded on Cell.  LP64 (ld), true 32-bit targets and the generic thunk
path are unchanged.

With Pmode DImode under ILP32 (0059), the same loads would be ld, reading
the 4-byte vtable pointer or offset together with the word after it.  Load
both in ptr_mode instead: that is lwz under ILP32 in either Pmode, and the
same Pmode load everywhere else.  The sign extension keys on ptr_mode for
the same reason.

Technique observed in the published GCC 4.1.1 PS3 toolchain sources.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000-call.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000-call.cc
@@ -2946,19 +2946,32 @@ rs6000_output_mi_thunk (FILE *file, tree thunk_fndecl ATTRIBUTE_UNUSED,
     {
       rtx vcall_offset_rtx = GEN_INT (vcall_offset);
       rtx tmp = gen_rtx_REG (Pmode, 12);
-
-      emit_move_insn (tmp, gen_rtx_MEM (Pmode, this_rtx));
+      /* The vtable pointer and the vcall offset are pointer-sized words.
+	 In the Cell ELF64/ILP32 ABI (TARGET_64BIT, ptr_mode SImode) they are
+	 4 bytes whichever mode addresses are formed in, so load them in
+	 ptr_mode: with Pmode DImode a Pmode load would also read the next
+	 word.  lwz zero-extends, which is right for the vtable pointer, an
+	 address, but the vcall offset is a signed displacement and is
+	 usually negative: added zero-extended, it carries into bit 32 of
+	 the adjusted `this'.  Sign-extend it first.  A separate extsw
+	 rather than lwa, which is microcoded on Cell.  */
+      rtx tmp_word = gen_rtx_REG (ptr_mode, 12);
+
+      emit_move_insn (tmp_word, gen_rtx_MEM (ptr_mode, this_rtx));
       if (((unsigned HOST_WIDE_INT) vcall_offset) + 0x8000 >= 0x10000)
 	{
 	  emit_insn (gen_add3_insn (tmp, tmp, vcall_offset_rtx));
-	  emit_move_insn (tmp, gen_rtx_MEM (Pmode, tmp));
+	  emit_move_insn (tmp_word, gen_rtx_MEM (ptr_mode, tmp));
 	}
       else
 	{
 	  rtx loc = gen_rtx_PLUS (Pmode, tmp, vcall_offset_rtx);
 
-	  emit_move_insn (tmp, gen_rtx_MEM (Pmode, loc));
+	  emit_move_insn (tmp_word, gen_rtx_MEM (ptr_mode, loc));
 	}
+      if (TARGET_64BIT && ptr_mode == SImode)
+	emit_insn (gen_rtx_SET (gen_rtx_REG (DImode, REGNO (tmp)),
+				gen_rtx_SIGN_EXTEND (DImode, tmp_word)));
       emit_insn (gen_add3_insn (this_rtx, this_rtx, tmp));
     }
 
